   "title": "Velocity Rig",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "# Velocity Rig: fast-paced camera-rig car race\nPick a **hero car**, a **rival car**, a **world** and a **camera rig**, press **Run**: one 2-4 s shot with LTX-2.5's own engine sound.\n\n**Rigs**: wheel cam (front / rear), door mount, bumper cam, rear bumper (reverse), roof cam, exhaust close-up,\narm car chase, arm car orbit, FPV drone dive / chase, top-down drone, helicopter wide, roadside whip pan,\nlow pass-by, crash zoom. **Worlds**: mountain pass, coastal cliffs, city night / day / tunnel, desert canyon,\nforest gravel, snow mountain, rain docklands, race circuit, or type your own.\n\n**Full race sequence**: leave rig on *auto (race sequence)*, set **shot_index** to *increment*, then queue 6-8 runs.\nEvery run advances the race arc (launch -> bumper draft -> hard brake -> wheel-cam hairpin -> FPV drift -> door-mount overtake -> reverse bumper defense -> whip-pan finish) and switches camera rigs."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 5,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    808,
    90
   ],
   "size": [
    460,
    144
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 0,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "First frame",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "**Z-Image Turbo** (8 steps) paints the opening frame exactly the way the rig sees the car: on the wheel arch, on the door, from the drone... LTX animates from this frame, so a strong first frame = a strong shot."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 16,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    2692,
    90
   ],
   "size": [
    560,
    144
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 0,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "Motion",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "**LTX-2.5 22B distilled**, image to video in two stages (half-res pass, x2 latent upscale, refine), with **synchronized audio**: the engine, tires and wind come from the same model. Size, length and fps all come from the rig node."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 49,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    4624,
    90
   ],
   "size": [
    460,
    188
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 0,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "Speed FX",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "**Velocity FX** adds what a real rig adds: vibration, radial speed blur that keeps the car sharp, crash zoom, lens fringing and speed ramps, using each rig's own defaults. Sliders at -1 follow the rig; strength 0 bypasses it. Frame count never changes, so the LTX audio stays in sync. Both the raw and the FX clip are saved."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
